 "summary": "The public surface is minimal: `CenteredClosedDisc.cayleyChart`, `ofDisc`, `center` and `mk` keep their bodies hidden behind characterising lemmas (`center_def`, `center_of_norm_eq_one`/`_ne_one`, `coe_mk`, `cayleyChart_source`/`_target`, `mem_atlas_iff`, `mem_halfDiscDom`), and the remaining `@[expose]` on the three atlases is needed for the `Fin 5`/`Fin 8` indexing in public statements. There is no compatibility layer and no misplaced general infrastructure.",
